            "response": "Do not rerun the response command or mark the feedback batch addressed.\n\nThe verified GitHub write remains credited against its pre-edit source revision: intent `migration-101`, IssueComment `IC_result201`, the exact request/body binding, and exact-reread receipt. Preserve that leaf receipt unchanged.\n\nNext:\n\n1. Free space without truncating or replacing any response-state files.\n2. Reconcile `migration-101` under the same intent key. Do not invoke another write.\n3. Append the recovered semantic outcome, linked to the surviving leaf receipt, once persistence is available.\n4. Start a fresh acquisition epoch because the reviewer edited the source after the write.\n5. Reacquire the complete paginated feedback state against the current PR head, then adjudicate the edited source as a new revision. Any further response requires separate current authority and a new independently bound intent where appropriate.\n\nNo response draft is authorized or needed in this step.\n\nDurable evidence must retain the original binding, attempt, leaf receipt, exact body digest and reread, the persistence failure, reconciliation record, recovered outcome, and the observed post-write source drift. Earlier evidence remains append-only.\n\nStopping state: the original response is `confirmed_success` for its preimage; semantic persistence requires reconciliation; the edited source is pending fresh acquisition and adjudication; the full batch is not addressed.",
