            "response": "Both responses are authorized, but they require separate one-intent invocations. The review\u2019s unrelated inline comments remain untouched.\n\n**Exact draft for IssueComment 81** \u2014 UTF-8, LF, no terminal newline:\n\n```json\n\"I documented the migration in the published revision, as [you requested](https://github.com/example/widgets/pull/418#issuecomment-81).\"\n```\n\n**Exact draft for PullRequestReview 82** \u2014 UTF-8, LF, no terminal newline:\n\n```json\n\"I recorded the benchmark\u2019s scope in the published revision, following [your review](https://github.com/example/widgets/pull/418#pullrequestreview-82).\"\n```\n\nFor each response independently:\n\n1. Bind the exact source revision, verified PR 418, head `1111111111111111111111111111111111111111`, adjudication, authority, and conversation placement.\n2. Record ambient client instructions as the writing policy; note that the separate review-voice route was unavailable.\n3. Freeze the body, writer identity, and SHA-256 digest.\n4. Immediately revalidate the source, relevant comments, PR head, authority, and body binding.\n5. Invoke `response_cli.py invoke` once using a distinct durable intent key.\n6. Record the authoritative leaf receipt, stable response identity, exact reread, and semantic outcome. An unknown result would require same-key reconciliation, never another write.\n\nNo dispatch was performed, so there are no receipt or outcome identities yet. The stopping state is two prepared, independently admissible conversation responses awaiting separate invocation and fresh pre-write revalidation.",
